      "evidence": "The displayed right inequality is asserted for every integer n>=1 and at n=1 contains integral_0^1 dt/t. The cited integral theorem requires integrable real functions on a closed interval, while def-natural-logarithm says log has domain exactly (0,infinity); 1/t is not a real-valued integrable function on [0,1]. Thus this half of 1.1 is undefined. It is also the inequality called on in 2.1 to obtain E_N>=0, although that conclusion instead follows from the left inequality.",
